# Search filters and manager

## Plugin semantics

Filters are declared via the Table’s search manager (e.g. `searchManager()` / behavior-backed configuration — follow the installed major’s API). Each filter maps request params to query conditions.

## Required behavior

- Inspect existing Table search configuration before adding filters.
- Use the narrowest filter type that matches the need (value, like, boolean, callback, etc. per docs).
- Keep callback filters focused; extract complex reusable query pieces to finders when appropriate.
- Align filter parameter names with forms/query strings used by the UI.

## Anti-patterns

- God callback filters that reimplement half the ORM
- Duplicate filter definitions across Tables without shared patterns the project already uses
